tess (docs): Hey team — I'm drafting a one-page "Concurrency & Errors" troubleshooting snippet for 429s, timeouts, and context-limit fallout. Need: two tiny SDK examples (py/js), a customer mitigation checklist, and a short migration note about trim helpers. Suggestions?

raj (eng-runtime): Shortlist: honor Retry-After if present; otherwise exponential backoff + full jitter; cap backoff (30s); after ~3 retries failover to lighter model or return a clear error. Note KV-cache cold starts can cause higher latency/timeouts — recommend a warmup or single retry with jitter.

emma (devex): I'll author the snippets. JS (AbortController + retry):```js
async function apiCallWithRetry(url, opts = {}, maxRetries = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i <= maxRetries; i++) {
    const ctrl = new AbortController();
    const timer = setTimeout(() => ctrl.abort(), opts.timeout || 60000);
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, { ...opts, signal: ctrl.signal });
      clearTimeout(timer);
      if (res.status === 429) {
        const ra = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
        const wait = ra ? Number(ra) : Math.min(Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random(), 30);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error('http error');
      return await res.json();
    } catch (err) {
      clearTimeout(timer);
      if (err.name === 'AbortError' && i < maxRetries) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, (Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random()) * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      throw err;
    }
  }
}
```

emma (devex): Python snippet (requests + jitter):```python
import time, random
import requests

def post_retry(url, payload, max_retries=3, timeout=60):
    for attempt in range(max_retries + 1):
        try:
            r = requests.post(url, json=payload, timeout=timeout)
            if r.status_code == 429:
                ra = r.headers.get('Retry-After')
                wait = int(ra) if ra and ra.isdigit() else min((2 ** attempt) + random.random(), 30)
                time.sleep(wait)
                continue
            r.raise_for_status()
            return r.json()
        except requests.RequestException:
            if attempt == max_retries:
                raise
            time.sleep((2 ** attempt) + random.random())
```

noah (support): Customer checklist to add: 1) If 429s spike after deploy, reduce max_response_tokens or trim history; 2) Limit client concurrency per user; 3) Try a quantized or smaller fallback model (eg redwood-lite); 4) For Dedicated customers, consider scaling pool; 5) Collect request ids + timestamps and open ticket.

tess (docs): Migration note: SDKs older than v1.3 exposed trim_history() which approximated tokens by message count. Newer SDKs provide trim_by_tokens() which uses the tokenizer — recommend updating and link to code sample.

raj (eng-runtime): Add wording: streaming can be truncated mid-token when forced truncation occurs; advise clients to handle incomplete chunks. Also include guidance to reduce batch size or prefill KV cache to avoid initial timeouts.

